- The class is annotated with `@CleanupTableInfo` targeting the open key, deleted, multipart info, and bucket tables.
- Per the class doc, the regular flow updates the multipart key with new part info, removes the open key, and moves any old or uncommitted key into the deleted table (see comment: `"If old key or uncommitted (pseudo) key exists, put it in DeletedTable"`).
- When the status is `NO_SUCH_MULTIPART_UPLOAD_ERROR`, the part is scheduled for deletion because the upload was aborted before commit; otherwise on `OK` it delegates to `addToDBBatch`.

